    "_build_note": {
      "before": "IRPT cell IB-rt-7 (PRD row B12, CTO ruling 3(b), slug row C-S73). THE HANDLER SERVES AND NEVER BUILDS: it reads the firm's landed HoldingsSnapshot and projects it to the resolved scope's permitted accounts through _authz.guard() + FirmBinding; a missing snapshot is UNAVAILABLE naming the as-of it looked for, never an inline run and never an empty success. THE ENTRY POINT IS snapshot.lambda_handler, not handler.lambda_handler: handler.py in this zip is the DIRECTORY (IB-s-1) handler, packaged flat and reused for its bucket map and its S3 directory read, so naming this module handler.py would have made `import handler` ambiguous on the runtime -- the same collision ops/ avoided with status.py. errors.py (_authz) and resolve.py (_scope) are packaged FLAT because every module sits at /var/task in a Lambda; both are staged from the COMMITTED blob by stage.py, which records each pin and sha256 in STAGE_MANIFEST.json -- a hand copy is a second definition with no vintage. enforce.py (_authz) is ALSO packaged FLAT but, since IRPT_BCKEND IB-rtf-8 (CTO ruling S82 @b37fdfd5cd), through the staged_from array above instead of stage.py's committed-copy mechanism: the committed copy went stale across the ruling @61627f39f9 with nobody noticing (the false-negative this cell's census demonstrates), and a build-time pinned stage cannot. ids.py, raw_keys.json, keys.py, firm_registry.json and jsonschema are NOT packaged here: they ride the shared irpt-common layer this function attaches (verified at this cell's cut to carry 9 of 9 declared members), and copying the ONE opaque-id normalizer beside a function is the defect IB-rt-3 removed. contracts/HoldingsSnapshot.schema.json IS packaged because the layer does not carry that contract at this cell's cut and this order's <paths> grant does not reach the layer (row IRPT_BCKEND-W1-S14); snapshot.py resolves /opt/python/irpt_contracts FIRST, so the day a cell adds it to the layer this copy stops being consulted with no edit here. NO LIVE VENDOR CALL: the only network call reachable from this function is s3:GetObject on the three client-firm buckets under investor-reporting/*. NO SCHEDULE, NO EVENT SOURCE, NO ALARM, NO SNS, NO SES.",
      "after": "Guarded entry.lambda_handler reads current publication index and version-pinned Platinum artifacts. Selection is reauthorized before and after retrieval. No Gold/pyarrow read dependency. Flat package proof checks canonical naming layout, pinned imports, selected read, corrupt-byte refusal and release revocation. Current runtime layer still supplies third-party dependencies; no deployed-layer qualification claimed."
    },
    "_staged_from_note": {
      "before": "IRPT_BCKEND IB-rte-4 (row W1-S20, the finding that opened this cell): served.py and loaders.py are declared and genuinely served but were never added to holdings/stage.py's own MEMBERS tuple (which already stages enforce.py/errors.py/resolve.py/handler.py the same way, committed). Rather than widen stage.py and commit two more flat copies under holdings/ (outside this order's BOUNDS, which touch only infra/aws/lambda/ci/), the same pinned-blob pattern is generalised into the shared builder: staged at build time from the _authz frontier, each blob's sha256 verified, never committed at the packaged path. IRPT_BCKEND IB-rtf-8 (CTO ruling S82 @b37fdfd5cd): enforce.py MOVED HERE from stage.py's committed-copy MEMBERS tuple -- the committed copy (blob 8f849457be) was `_authz/enforce.py` as it stood at commit 28ccac62c9, PRE-DATING the CTO's own project-first fix at @61627f39f9 (the fold's own diff: 20 lines only-in-fork, 61 only-in-shared, all of it the superseded pre-fix refusal order and the disclosure-field plumbing that never followed it), and nobody re-ran stage.py to catch it -- exactly the staleness the note above already named for served.py/loaders.py. enforce.py now shares their remedy: staged at build time from the _authz frontier, sha256-verified against a blob pinned at THIS cell's HEAD, never committed at the packaged path, so it cannot go stale again without the pin itself moving.",
      "after": "IRPT MVP P: exact canonical shared selection/auth/IDs, versioned holdings reader, and naming dependencies pinned with blob hashes. Nested lib and registry/schema layout preserved; flat opal_naming forwards canonical address/lookup only. Source declaration, not deployment metadata."
    },
